<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  VisionPilot on AUTOSAR Adaptive (CAPI) — service interfaces.

  Four interfaces, all event-only. There are no methods anywhere in this model:
  every exchange is a periodic stream where only the newest value matters, which
  is what an Event is for. A Field would add last-value semantics nothing needs;
  a Method would add a round trip inside a 50 ms control period.

  The four boundaries follow the reference AD decomposition — Sensing,
  Perception, Planning, Control — one Adaptive Application each:

    CameraFrameService    sensingd    -> perceptiond    frame descriptor
    DrivingStateService   perceptiond -> planningd      fused lane/CIPO state
    TrajectoryService     planningd   -> controld       acceleration + steering horizon
    VehicleStatusService  controld    -> planningd      ego speed

  Localization is absent, deliberately and visibly. VisionPilot estimates a
  lane-relative state, not a map pose; on the rover /odom exists and nothing
  consumes it. A Localization AA would slot between Sensing and Perception if
  one is ever written, and no interface here pretends to be it.

  ===========================================================================
  Why Sensing is its own AA even though a frame is 3 MB

  Sensing is the abstraction over sensors — camera today, radar and lidar later.
  Folding it into Perception would save bandwidth and destroy the layer that
  makes a new sensor a new provided port rather than an edit inside Perception.
  The abstraction is worth more than the bytes.

  The bytes are handled by not sending them. Sensing owns a shared-memory ring;
  each frame is written into a slot and only the FrameDescriptor (34 B) travels
  through ara::com. Perception maps the same segment read-only. The interface is
  fully modelled; only the buffer transport is not.

  Payload class, not sensor type, picks the transport. Camera and lidar are
  large and get the descriptor + shared-memory pattern; radar detections are a
  bounded list of a few KB and would go over SOME/IP directly, with no shared
  memory at all. The interface shape stays uniform either way.

  WHAT THIS COSTS, stated plainly because the ARXML cannot express it:
    - E2E protection covers the descriptor, never the pixels. A payload
      integrity check has to be the ring's own (generation + CRC in the slot
      header).
    - IAM does not gate access to the segment. Filesystem permissions on the
      /dev/shm object do, which means the user and resource group EM starts each
      process under are load-bearing — see the deployment manifest.
    - It is a documented architectural deviation, not something a reviewer can
      find by reading the model alone.

  On the Orin the better form is a DMA-buf pool allocated once at startup, with
  FDs exchanged a single time over a unix socket and the per-frame event
  carrying only the slot index — the same descriptor, with the frame never
  touching host memory. An FD is not serialisable, so it can never ride the
  event itself.
  ===========================================================================

  There is no gateway AA. A gateway bridges two middlewares; with ROS 2 removed
  from the perception and planning path there is no second middleware, and the
  chassis is a device that Control drives directly.

  Unit mismatch to resolve OUTSIDE this model: Trajectory carries a
  bicycle-model pair (tyre angle in rad, acceleration in m/s^2) and the ESP32
  accepts a velocity pair ({'T':13,'X':linear,'Z':angular}). The conversion
  belongs in Control, which is the component that knows the vehicle model — not
  here, and not in Planning.
-->
<AUTOSAR xmlns="http://autosar.org/schema/r4.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://autosar.org/schema/r4.0 AUTOSAR_00049.xsd">
  <AR-PACKAGES>
    <AR-PACKAGE>
      <SHORT-NAME>AvServiceInterfaces</SHORT-NAME>
      <ELEMENTS>

        <SERVICE-INTERFACE>
          <SHORT-NAME>CameraFrameService</SHORT-NAME>
          <DESC>
            <L-2 L="EN">Camera frames offered by the Sensing AA as shared-memory references. Carries no pixel data.</L-2>
          </DESC>
          <NAMESPACES>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>av</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>av</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>vp</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>vp</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>cm</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>cm</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
          </NAMESPACES>
          <MAJOR-VERSION>1</MAJOR-VERSION>
          <MINOR-VERSION>0</MINOR-VERSION>
          <EVENTS>
            <VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
              <SHORT-NAME>FrameEvent</SHORT-NAME>
              <DESC><L-2 L="EN">One capture: BEV-warped and plain-resized images, referenced by ring slot. Both travel in one sample because they share an exposure.</L-2></DESC>
              <TYPE-TREF DEST="STD-CPP-IMPLEMENTATION-DATA-TYPE">/AvTypes/DataTypes/FrameDescriptor</TYPE-TREF>
            </VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
          </EVENTS>
        </SERVICE-INTERFACE>

        <SERVICE-INTERFACE>
          <SHORT-NAME>DrivingStateService</SHORT-NAME>
          <DESC>
            <L-2 L="EN">Fused lane-relative state and CIPO estimate produced by the Perception AA.</L-2>
          </DESC>
          <NAMESPACES>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>av</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>av</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>vp</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>vp</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>cm</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>cm</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
          </NAMESPACES>
          <MAJOR-VERSION>1</MAJOR-VERSION>
          <MINOR-VERSION>0</MINOR-VERSION>
          <EVENTS>
            <VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
              <SHORT-NAME>DrivingStateEvent</SHORT-NAME>
              <DESC><L-2 L="EN">Exactly what Planner::compute_plan consumes, less ego speed.</L-2></DESC>
              <TYPE-TREF DEST="STD-CPP-IMPLEMENTATION-DATA-TYPE">/AvTypes/DataTypes/DrivingState</TYPE-TREF>
            </VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
          </EVENTS>
        </SERVICE-INTERFACE>

        <SERVICE-INTERFACE>
          <SHORT-NAME>TrajectoryService</SHORT-NAME>
          <DESC>
            <L-2 L="EN">Planned trajectory from the Planning AA, consumed by Control.</L-2>
          </DESC>
          <NAMESPACES>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>av</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>av</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>vp</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>vp</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>cm</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>cm</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
          </NAMESPACES>
          <MAJOR-VERSION>1</MAJOR-VERSION>
          <MINOR-VERSION>0</MINOR-VERSION>
          <EVENTS>
            <VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
              <SHORT-NAME>TrajectoryEvent</SHORT-NAME>
              <DESC><L-2 L="EN">Acceleration plus the full 20-step steering horizon, so Control has something to follow when planning stops.</L-2></DESC>
              <TYPE-TREF DEST="STD-CPP-IMPLEMENTATION-DATA-TYPE">/AvTypes/DataTypes/Trajectory</TYPE-TREF>
            </VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
          </EVENTS>
        </SERVICE-INTERFACE>

        <SERVICE-INTERFACE>
          <SHORT-NAME>VehicleStatusService</SHORT-NAME>
          <DESC>
            <L-2 L="EN">Ego vehicle state sensed by the Control AA and consumed by Planning.</L-2>
          </DESC>
          <NAMESPACES>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>av</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>av</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>vp</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>vp</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
            <SYMBOL-PROPS><SHORT-NAME>cm</SHORT-NAME><SYMBOL>cm</SYMBOL></SYMBOL-PROPS>
          </NAMESPACES>
          <MAJOR-VERSION>1</MAJOR-VERSION>
          <MINOR-VERSION>0</MINOR-VERSION>
          <EVENTS>
            <VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
              <SHORT-NAME>SpeedEvent</SHORT-NAME>
              <DESC><L-2 L="EN">Ego longitudinal speed, m/s.</L-2></DESC>
              <TYPE-TREF DEST="STD-CPP-IMPLEMENTATION-DATA-TYPE">/AvTypes/DataTypes/VehicleSpeed</TYPE-TREF>
            </VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
          </EVENTS>
        </SERVICE-INTERFACE>

      </ELEMENTS>
    </AR-PACKAGE>
  </AR-PACKAGES>
</AUTOSAR>
